<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adherbal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 112 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adherbal was a king of Numidia, the elder son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/micipsa">Micipsa</a>, who shared the kingdom from 118 BCE with his brother Hiempsal and his adoptive brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a>. After Hiempsal's murder he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, which divided Numidia between him and Jugurtha. Jugurtha besieged him in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirta">Cirta</a> and put him to death in 112 BCE, together with the Italian traders there, provoking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war">Jugurthine War</a>.</p></div>
